    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-yusuf">Qara Yusuf</a> returned from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> captivity to defeat the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurids</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakhchivan">Nakhchivan</a> in 1406 and Sardrud in 1408, and by taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> in 1410 freed the Qara Qoyunlu from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalayirid-sultanate">Jalayirids</a>.</li><li>Jahan Shah (1436–1467) became independent on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-rukh">Shah Rukh</a>'s death in 1447, conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazd">Yazd</a> in 1452–1453 and occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herat">Herat</a> for some months in 1458.</li><li>The Qara Qoyunlu court wrote to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurids</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in Persian and to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a> in Arabic, and Jahan Shah styled himself Padishah-i <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, King of Kings of Iran.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quli-qutb-mulk">Sultan Quli</a>, founder of the Qutb Shahi Sultanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golconda-fort">Golconda</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1518, was a fourth-generation descendant of the Qara Qoyunlu ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-iskander">Qara Iskander</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

