t.</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="372.3" x2="372.3" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="372.3" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="372.3" y="164" text-anchor="middle">5</text><title>1420: Qara Yusuf dies in December; his sons fight for the succession and Shah Rukh invades, occupying Tabriz briefly in 1421.</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="579.1" x2="579.1" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="579.1" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="579.1" y="164" text-anchor="middle">6</text><title>1447: On Shah Rukh's death Jahan Shah throws off Timurid vassalage, takes the titles sultan and khan and seizes Sultaniya, Hamadan and Qazvin.</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="663.4" x2="663.4" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="663.4" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="663.4" y="164" text-anchor="middle">7</text><title>1458: Jahan Shah advances to Herat and holds the Timurid capital for some months, until Hasan Ali's revolt and Abu Said's march on Tabriz force him back.</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="732.3" x2="732.3" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="732.3" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="732.3" y="164" text-anchor="middle">8</text><title>1467: Jahan Shah is killed at the Battle of Chapakchur after his failed attack on Aq Qoyunlu Diyarbakır; by 1468 Uzun Hasan has conquered Iraq, Azerbaijan and western Iran.</title></g><text class="rf-axis" x="20" y="200">1374 CE</text><text class="rf-axis" x="740" y="200" text-anchor="end">1468 CE</text></svg><figcaption>Relative power on the Institute's 0–10 scale (each profile scaled to its own peak). Numbers mark the key events below.</figcaption></figure><ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">1384</span><span class="rf-text">Qara Mahammad invades <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mardin">Mardin</a> and takes the submission of its Artuqid ruler Majd al-Din Isa, who becomes a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1400</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> defeats the Qara Qoyunlu; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-yusuf">Qara Yusuf</a> flees to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a>, where an-Nasir Faraj imprisons him together with the Jalayirid sultan Ahmad.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1408</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-yusuf">Qara Yusuf</a> crushes the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurids</a> Abu Bakr and Miran Shah at the Battle of Sardrud on 20 April; Miran Shah is killed.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1410</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-yusuf">Qara Yusuf</a> conquers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a>, executes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaykh-uways">Shaykh Uways</a> Jalayir, captures <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> and takes control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>; the Qara Qoyunlu are independent.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1420</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-yusuf">Qara Yusuf</a> dies in December; his sons fight for the succession and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-rukh">Shah Rukh</a> invades, occupying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> briefly in 1421.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1447</span><span class="rf-text">On <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-rukh">Shah Rukh</a>'s death Jahan Shah throws off Timurid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassalage</a>, takes the titles sultan and khan and seizes Sultaniya, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamadan">Hamadan</a> and Qazvin.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1458</span><span class="rf-text">Jahan Shah advances to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herat">Herat</a> and holds the Timurid capital for some months, until Hasan Ali's revolt and Abu Said's march on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> force him back.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1467</span><span class="rf-text">Jahan Shah is killed at the Battle of Chapakchur after his failed attack on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a> Diyarbakır; by 1468 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzun-hasan">Uzun Hasan</a> has conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>.</span></li></ol>
